(Bug #76's fix hoisted four copies of one type table into one. These are
 the sibling arms that were already right — a list, a buffer, a text and a
 value parameter, and a top-level map read outside any function. They must
 answer exactly as they did before, or the hoist changed more than the one
 missing `map` row it was written to add.)

To 'describe the marks' with a list called marks.
    Print marks's length,
    Print marks,
    Print marks's type.

To 'describe the greeting' with a buffer called greeting.
    Print greeting's size,
    Print greeting's empty,
    Print greeting's type.

To 'describe the caption' with a text called caption.
    Print caption,
    Print caption's type.

To 'describe whatever arrives' with a value called arrival.
    Print arrival,
    Print arrival's type.

A list called marks is [1, 2].
'describe the marks' of marks.

A buffer called greeting is "hello".
'describe the greeting' of greeting.

'describe the caption' of "plain".
'describe whatever arrives' of 7.

A map called 'the class' is {"ada": 1, "bea": 2}.
Print 'the class''s length.
Print 'the class'.
Exit 0.
